{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-normalization}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a72c35e962fe818ae1fed5dbc75647847ff033ac081cc239c641e9aeae04f543", "source_text": "Normalization", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb8c714748af8e44825a3f4b88b4d6ac168c966108dd836c3e8960ddaed09bc8", "unit_id": "tag:035E:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X^{(0)} \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-generic-points}\nf :\nY = \\coprod\\nolimits_{\\eta \\in X^{(0)}} \\Spec(\\kappa(\\eta))\n\\longrightarrow\nX\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-points}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-section-separation-axioms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fa8462f714fc85768b26bcae10fbddb9a7330d27968535a0042b5a85bce15b8e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:841b820379f7700c0f3b2a5e8c972613b44d13d2f7050b9ddcbd4fe6ea912152", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we come to the normalization of a scheme <MATH_0001>.\nWe only define/construct it when <MATH_0002> has locally finitely many irreducible\ncomponents. Let <MATH_0003> be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has\nfinitely many irreducible components. Let\n<MATH_0004> be the set of generic points of irreducible components\nof <MATH_0005>. Let\n<MATH_0006>\nbe the inclusion of the generic points into <MATH_0007> using the\ncanonical maps of Schemes, Section <REF_0001>.\nNote that this morphism is quasi-compact by assumption and\nquasi-separated as <MATH_0008> is separated (see\nSchemes, Section <REF_0002>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be38382ccd1a98cbac4cea82faad610e60f6254d74d49cfb6c2dc641026bc757", "unit_id": "tag:035E:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\nu : X^\\nu \\longrightarrow X\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$f : Y \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-generic-points}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-normalization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d89aa92365f970936efb73aaa4f4457118fde19279c958a5d65482f2d82b3925", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0386abeaf2e9c4200d3b682ef9b3a284129a00d50feca6a2dbbe979b09dd47af", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has\nfinitely many irreducible components. We define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>normalization<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> as the morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich is the normalization of <MATH_0004> in the morphism <MATH_0005>\n(<REF_0001>) constructed above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f8b7e4a1d995408d21557175d41fef3cde51e78131e1508c2aadcc544c26201", "unit_id": "tag:035N:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_{red}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e8302a83568d3b87b59c371c5cbbed21f982d02e23d2f416ef212c6a04e41341", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f7ad611a75800ab66dfe18496966dafcaaef66efff0cf19021062738ec64db8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAny locally Noetherian scheme has a locally finite set of irreducible\ncomponents and the definition applies to it.\nUsually the normalization is defined only for reduced schemes.\nWith the definition above the normalization of <MATH_0001> is the same\nas the normalization of the reduction <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:535740eae82d596df70fe3ae1d21b6fac3d0964764a8e43f8a5ca46092582065", "unit_id": "tag:035E:prose-0002"}
